#: docs/tutorials/customize.md:3
msgid ""
"`rsdk` uses [`devenv`](https://devenv.sh/) to manage its **dev**elopment "
"**env**rionronment, but itself is not `nix` based. `nix` has good support "
"generating `NixOS` images, but here we are dealing with a Debian system, and "
"some parts are [currently "
"missing](https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pull/270095)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/customize.md:5
msgid ""
"We currently uses [`bdebstrap`](https://github.com/bdrung/bdebstrap), which "
"is a YAML frontend for "
"[`mmdebstrap`](https://gitlab.mister-muffin.de/josch/mmdebstrap). "
"`mmdebstrap` is [the recommended "
"tool](https://wiki.debian.org/RISC-V#Creating_a_riscv64_chroot) for building "
"RISC-V systems compared to traditional `debootstrap`."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/customize.md:7
msgid ""
"YAML itself is not a templating language, so it cannot dynamically generate "
"different configurations for different builds. We use "
"[`jsonnet`](https://jsonnet.org) for this purpose."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/customize.md:9
msgid ""
"Lastly, `mmdebstrap` does not handle disk image generation. We again use "
"`jsonnet` to dynamically generate a "
"[`guestfish`](https://libguestfs.org/guestfish.1.html) script to handle this "
"task."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/customize.md:11
msgid ""
"All of those tools are glued by `bash` to provide a frontend, known as "
"[`rsdk-build`](https://github.com/RadxaOS-SDK/rsdk/tree/main/src/libexec/rsdk/rsdk-build)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/customize.md:13
msgid ""
"Depending on your goal, you would need the knowledge of some of the above "
"tools."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/customize.md:15
msgid "Rootfs customization"
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/customize.md:17
msgid ""
"[`rootfs.jsonnet`](https://github.com/RadxaOS-SDK/rsdk/tree/main/src/share/rsdk/build/rootfs.jsonnet) "
"is the entry point for rootfs template. It collects the various inputs and "
"passes them to different modules."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/customize.md:19
msgid ""
"Module loading order matters, as that will determine "
"[`*-hooks`](https://manpages.debian.org/testing/mmdebstrap/mmdebstrap.1.en.html#HOOKS)'s "
"execution order. The safest way is to only edit the `customize-hooks` field "
"in `rootfs.jsonnet` and only adding new entries after the existing ones."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/customize.md:21
msgid ""
"You can also edit the `packages` field in `rootfs.jsonnet` to add additional "
"packages to the system. `customize-hooks` will be run after `packages` are "
"installed in the rootfs."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/customize.md:23
msgid ""
"Checkout [`Work with local packages`](local_pkg.md#rsdk-build---debs) if you "
"have local packages to install."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/customize.md:25
msgid "Disk image customization"
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/customize.md:27
msgid ""
"[`image.jsonnet`](https://github.com/RadxaOS-SDK/rsdk/tree/main/src/share/rsdk/build/rootfs.jsonnet) "
"is the template for the deployment script. It is generally not necessary to "
"change this part."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:3
msgid ""
"Every device supported by RadxaOS requires several metapackages available in "
"the apt repositories. They are usually unique to each hardware, as such "
"cannot be shared between devices."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:7
msgid ""
"It is intentional to keep this info in form of package dependencies, and "
"spread out in several packages, instead of a single hard coded config file. "
"This is because:"
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:10
msgid ""
"Different build tools don't need to track this config in order to build with "
"correct packages."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:12
msgid ""
"Ease of migration between tools.  \n"
"For example, from `rbuild` to `rsdk`, we use the same simple package logic "
"instead doing data transform, which was the case for `rbuild`'s `configs` "
"files."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:16
msgid "Allow underlying package to be changed/updated in the future."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:18
msgid "Adding new device"
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:20
msgid "Currently, there are 4 places that need to be updated:"
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:22
msgid ""
"Kernel metapackages  \n"
"Those includes Linux kernel image as well as kernel header, and some other "
"less used packages.  \n"
"Currently you need to edit the related `bsp` [Linux "
"profile](https://github.com/radxa-repo/bsp/blob/main/linux/latest/fork.conf) "
"to include the new device."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:28
msgid ""
"Firmware metapackage  \n"
"This is similar to the kernel package in case of U-Boot, where the [U-Boot "
"profile](https://github.com/radxa-repo/bsp/blob/main/u-boot/latest/fork.conf) "
"needs to be updated.  \n"
"For EDK2 you will need to [add the "
"metapackage](https://github.com/radxa-pkg/edk2-cix/blob/main/debian/control) "
"in the related repo."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:34
msgid ""
"Product metapackage  \n"
"Each product also needs its own package to pull device-specific drivers, and "
"some common config options. Those are defined in "
"[`radxa-profiles`](https://github.com/radxa-pkg/radxa-profiles/blob/main/debian/control) "
"repo."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:39
msgid ""
"[`products.json`](https://github.com/RadxaOS-SDK/rsdk/blob/main/src/share/rsdk/configs/products.json) "
" \n"
"This registers the supported products for `rsdk` and their default "
"configurations."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:42
msgid ""
"Right now, product metapackage does not specify dependencies to kernel and "
"firmware (even though we have product-agnostic metapackages for those two). "
"This is to allow users to install custom kernels only without breaking the "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:47
msgid ""
"Note that vendor metapackage is listed as recommended in product "
"metapackages. This way users can install the system without SoC vendors' "
"binary packages."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:50
msgid ""
"Finally, create the new product build repo under "
"[`radxa-build`](https://github.com/radxa-build) with "
"`rsdk-infra-product-update` command."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:53
msgid "What if we introduce a new SoC?"
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:55 docs/tutorials/new_device.md:75
msgid "You need to additionally update following places:"
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:57
msgid ""
"Vendor metapackage  \n"
"Each SoC needs their own package to pull SoC-specific packages, and some "
"common config options. Those are defined in "
"[`vendor-profiles`](https://github.com/radxa-pkg/vendor-profiles/blob/main/debian/control) "
"repo."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:62
msgid ""
"[`socs.json`](https://github.com/RadxaOS-SDK/rsdk/blob/main/src/share/rsdk/configs/socs.json) "
" \n"
"New SoC **MUST** be added to `soc_specific_repo` array as well."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:64
msgid ""
"New SoC-specific apt repo under "
"[`radxa-repo`](https://github.com/radxa-repo) organization."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:65
msgid ""
"SoC-specific package repo  \n"
"In case of Rockchip, those are managed by "
"[`rockchip-prebuilt`](https://github.com/radxa-pkg/rockchip-prebuilt) repo, "
"and we create Rockchip SDK prebuilt packages in GitHub Releases, which will "
"be uploaded to the SoC-specific apt repo.  \n"
"If the new SoC is only a variant of already supported SoC, then you only "
"need to edit the related "
"[`pkg.conf`](https://github.com/radxa-pkg/rockchip-prebuilt/blob/main/pkg.conf.linux-6.1-stan-rkr1) "
"to include the new SoC-specific apt repo."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:73
msgid "What if we introduce a new SoC vendor?"
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:77
msgid ""
"Vendor metapackage  \n"
"Each vendor needs their own package to pull common config options. Those are "
"defined in "
"[`vendor-profiles`](https://github.com/radxa-pkg/vendor-profiles/blob/main/debian/control) "
"repo."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/new_device.md:81
msgid ""
"[`socs.json`](https://github.com/RadxaOS-SDK/rsdk/blob/main/src/share/rsdk/configs/socs.json) "
" \n"
"There should be a new item for the new vendor."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/global_options.md:3
msgid ""
"Like [`rbuild`](https://radxa-repo.github.io/rbuild/dev/config.html), `rsdk` "
"also allows defining global build options. The underlying mechanical is the "
"same: predefined environmental variables. However, since we use `devenv` to "
"manage the environment, the way to define them is also changed."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/global_options.md:8
msgid ""
"For now, you will need to add your definitions in `devenv.local.nix` file. "
"We provide `devenv.local.nix.example` as a reference for file structure. "
"This is also what we use in the office, but the server is locally hosted, so "
"you won't be able to use it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/global_options.md:13
msgid "Example: set up local apt cache to speed up build"
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/global_options.md:15
msgid ""
"If you want to speed up image building time, one way is to use a locally "
"hosted apt cache to reduce download time."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/global_options.md:18
msgid ""
"First, copy `devenv.local.nix.example` to `devenv.local.nix`. You can then "
"remove `RSDK_OPTION_REPO_SUFFIX` if you do not want to build test image by "
"default, and then change `RSDK_OPTION_*_MIRROR` to your own address. Typical "
"options are:"
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/global_options.md:22
msgid ""
"`RSDK_OPTION_DISTRO_MIRROR`: default Debian/Ubuntu mirror (equivalent to "
"`rsdk build -m`)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/global_options.md:23
msgid ""
"`RSDK_OPTION_RADXA_MIRROR`: default Radxa APT mirror for radxa-deb "
"(equivalent to `rsdk build -M`)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/tutorials/global_options.md:25
msgid ""
"When using Radxa repositories, `rsdk` will use Radxa `pkgs.json` metadata by "
"default whenever it is available. You can disable this behavior at build "
"time by passing `-P`/`--no-pkgs-json` or by setting "
"`RSDK_OPTION_PKGS_JSON=false` explicitly in the environment."
msgstr ""

